-- The quiescence drain's remaining `DrainDiags` member (`compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`).
--
-- `relay`'s inferred scheme quantifies `a` and carries both `Tweak a Int` and
-- `Tweak a Bool`.  The diagnostics-arm drain replays the call `value n x` with that
-- goal PROJECTED to its first argument and `a` reading `Float`, so the selector sees
-- `Tweak Float`, which both instances match with no stable minimum, and reports
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  Not the #3031 shape: the goal reaches the drain ground, so
-- no closedness test can defer it.  `DrainRollback` discards it on `check`; the
-- trees-arm drain of `run` and `build` does not produce it.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived: `relay`'s goals belong to its callers; `main` calls it at
-- `Float`, where `Tweak Float Int` and `Tweak Float Bool` are each the unique match.
-- `relay 1 2.5` = `value 1 2.5` = `tweak True (tweak 1 (relay 0 2.5))` = 2.5, since
-- both impls return their second argument.  ACCEPT on every verb, printing `2.5`.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must not report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  Today that holds
-- only because `DrainRollback` hides the drain's diagnostics; it is the witness that
-- must stay green when `DrainDiags` is deleted.
interface Tweak a b where
  tweak : b -> a -> a

impl Tweak Float Int where
  tweak _ x = x

impl Tweak Float Bool where
  tweak _ x = x

value : (Tweak a Int, Tweak a Bool) => Int -> a -> a
value n x = if n == 0 then x else tweak True (tweak 1 (relay (n - 1) x))

relay n x = value n x

main = println (relay 1 (2.5 : Float))
